In order to ascertain such declaration, the factors that need to be considered inter alia are knowledge or recognition obtained by way of promotion of the said trademark, duration,
extent and geographical area of use of the said Section 11(6)-The Registrar shall, while determining whether a trade mark is a well-known trade mark, take into account any fact which he considers relevant for determining a trade mark as a well-known trade mark including-- (i) the knowledge or recognition of that trade mark in the relevant section of the public including knowledge in India obtained as a result of promotion of the trade mark;
(ii) the duration, extent and geographical area of any use of that trade mark;
